Context                                                                                                                                                                   The single-match E2E test is fully passing — 17/17 deliveries sync from Flutter UI to PostgreSQL via the sync          service, match result and awards are correctly computed. All sync bugs (RC1-RC4) are fixed. See  docs/CONTINUE_PROMPT.md for full history.                                                                                                                                                                                                     Goal                                                                                                                                                                      Set up and test real-time ball-by-ball score viewing from a second device/emulator while scoring a match on the first   device. The server broadcasts WebSocket messages to all subscribers in a match


room.
  Key Files to Read First

  Server-side WebSocket:
  - apps/server/src/websocket/handler.ts — WebSocket connection handler, join_match / leave_match message processing
  - apps/server/src/websocket/rooms.ts — buildScoreUpdate(), buildWicketMessage(), buildMatchCompleteMessage(),
  getMatchState()
  - apps/server/src/websocket/broadcaster.ts — broadcastScoreUpdate(), broadcastWicket(), broadcastInningsComplete(),
  broadcastMatchComplete()
  - apps/server/src/types/websocket.ts — All WebSocket message type definitions (ScoreUpdateMessage, WicketMessage,
  etc.)

  Flutter client-side viewer:
  - apps/mobile/lib/src/features/scoring/presentation/notifiers/match_live_notifier.dart — MatchLiveNotifier,
  LiveMatchState, WebSocket connection logic
  - apps/mobile/lib/src/features/scoring/providers.dart — matchLiveNotifierProvider

  Scoring route (broadcasts happen here):
  - apps/server/src/routes/v1/scoring.ts — Lines 125-250, after recordDelivery() succeeds, broadcasts score_update,
  wicket, innings_complete, match_complete

  WebSocket Connection Info

  - URL: ws://localhost:3001/ws (from same machine) or ws://10.0.2.2:3001/ws (from Android emulator)
  - Join a match room: Send {"type":"join_match","matchId":"<id>"}
  - Server responds with: Full match state snapshot, then real-time score_update, wicket, innings_complete,
  match_complete messages as deliveries are scored

  Testing Options to Explore

  1. Second Android emulator — Launch a second AVD, install the app, navigate to match viewer
  2. Simple HTML/JS WebSocket client — Create a minimal ws-viewer.html that connects and renders live score (serve via
  npx http-server)
  3. wscat CLI — npx wscat -c ws://localhost:3001/ws then send join_match JSON manually to see raw messages
  4. Physical device — Connect phone on same network, use server's LAN IP

